DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Digital Archives
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to the online digital collection of the Maine State Ar
 chives\, a bureau within the Department of the Secretary of State. We main
 tain approximately 8 miles of official state records (both paper and digit
 al) that are deemed permanently valuable. These records include bills intr
 oduced in the Legislature\, reports from the Governor's Executive Council\
 , election returns\, deeds and maps from the Maine Land Office\, vital sta
 tistics prior to 1892\, federal census records up to 1880\, county court r
 ecords dating back to 1636\, and military records through World War I\, am
 ong others.\nAs of March 1\, 2026\, our online collection includes over on
 e million individual records. The Maine State Archives will continue to ex
 pand this database as we digitize more of our collection. All documents ar
 e public records and are free to download. To begin your search\, check th
 e following sources:\nDigital Archives Portal\n: Open Access - online digi
 tal collection of the Maine State Archives.\nArchivesSpace Public Interfac
 e\n: Use this database to search through the archival findings aids\, coll
 ection structures\, and descriptions of physical and digital records manag
 ed by the bureau.\nUser Guide\nMaine Memory Network\n: A digital history p
 latform featuring specific exhibits\, historical photographs\, and selecte
 d primary documents contributed by the Maine State Archives.\nFamily Searc
 h\n: FamilySearch is the world’s largest free genealogy resource.\nHarmf
 ul Content Advisory (PDF)\nhttps://www.maine.gov/sos/archives/digital-arch
 ives
URL:https://www.maine.gov/sos/archives/digital-archives
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
